# Code Review Checklist

## Pre-Review Requirements

### Code Quality
- [ ] TypeScript compilation passes without errors or warnings
- [ ] All code follows [biome.jsonc](mdc:frontend/biome.jsonc) formatting standards
- [ ] ESLint passes with no violations
- [ ] No console.log statements in production code
- [ ] All functions have proper type definitions

### Architecture & Patterns
- [ ] Follows established patterns in [frontend/app](mdc:frontend/app) structure
- [ ] Components are properly composed and reusable
- [ ] Business logic is separated from UI components
- [ ] Uses appropriate React patterns (hooks, context, etc.)
- [ ] API calls use proper error handling and loading states

### Security & Data Handling
- [ ] All user inputs are validated with Zod schemas
- [ ] Database queries use proper RLS policies
- [ ] No sensitive data exposed in client-side code
- [ ] Authentication flows are secure and tested
- [ ] File uploads properly validated and secured

### Performance & Optimization
- [ ] No unnecessary re-renders or expensive computations
- [ ] Images optimized and properly sized
- [ ] Bundle impact analyzed for new dependencies
- [ ] Server-side rendering used where appropriate
- [ ] Database queries are optimized

### Testing & Validation
- [ ] Critical paths have test coverage
- [ ] Edge cases and error scenarios handled
- [ ] Loading and error states implemented
- [ ] Accessibility requirements met
- [ ] Cross-browser compatibility verified

### Documentation & Maintenance
- [ ] Code is self-documenting with clear naming
- [ ] Complex logic has explanatory comments
- [ ] API changes documented
- [ ] Migration scripts provided if needed
- [ ] Environment variables updated in [.env.example](mdc:frontend/.env.example)

## Database & Migration Checklist
- [ ] Migration scripts are reversible
- [ ] Data integrity maintained during schema changes
- [ ] RLS policies updated for new tables/columns
- [ ] Performance impact of changes assessed
- [ ] Backup strategy considered

## Deployment Readiness
- [ ] Changes work with current [docker-compose.yml](mdc:docker-compose.yml) setup
- [ ] Environment-specific configurations handled
- [ ] No breaking changes without migration path
- [ ] Rollback plan available
- [ ] Monitoring/logging implemented for new features

## Anti-Patterns to Reject
- ❌ Temporary fixes or TODO comments for production issues
- ❌ Hard-coded values that should be configurable
- ❌ Copy-pasted code without proper abstraction
- ❌ Missing error handling or user feedback
- ❌ Database queries without proper indexing
- ❌ Unused imports or dependencies
- ❌ Overly complex components that should be split
- ❌ Missing TypeScript types or any type usage

## Review Focus Areas

### For Components
- Proper props validation and TypeScript interfaces
- Accessibility attributes and keyboard navigation
- Responsive design implementation
- Error boundary coverage

### For API Routes
- Input validation and sanitization
- Proper HTTP status codes
- Error responses with meaningful messages
- Rate limiting and security headers

### For Database Changes
- Migration safety and reversibility
- Index creation for performance
- RLS policy completeness
- Data validation constraints

### For Configuration
- Environment variable management
- Security of sensitive configurations
- Documentation of new settings
- Backward compatibility
